# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated data, results and artifacts -- NEVER commit these
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Ignored by DIRECTORY, not only by extension. The extension rules further down
# (*.csv, *.parquet, *.json, *.png) already catch most of what lands here, but
# they are the wrong guarantee: one .pkl of prediction outputs, one .pt
# checkpoint, one .npy, and it is committed forever. That is not hypothetical
# -- it is how a sibling research repo reached 6 GB, 98% of it pickled model
# outputs under a data/ directory, with the actual code at 219 MB.
#
# Everything below is REGENERATED by the pipeline and reproducible from code:
#   data/     downloaded + built parquet datasets   (~200 MB)
#   results/  forecasts, per-period tables, metrics (~770 MB, mostly forecasts)
#   models/   fitted live estimators, rewritten every refit
#   logs/     per-run build and training logs
/data/*
/results/
/models/
/logs/

# Screen session logs (screen -L -Logfile <name>.txt) land at the repo root.
*.txt
# ...but a handful of root .txt files are real content, not run output. Without
# these negations a requirements.txt would be silently absent from the push.
!LICENSE.txt
!requirements.txt
!requirements-*.txt

# Byte-compiled / optimized / DLL files
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# C extensions
*.so

# Distribution / packaging
.Python
/env/
/build/
develop-eggs/
/dist/
/downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
/lib/
/lib64/
parts/
sdist/
/var/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg

# PyInstaller
#  Usually these files are written by a python script from a template
#  before PyInstaller builds the exe, so as to inject date/other infos into it.
*.manifest
*.spec

# Installer logs
pip-log.txt
pip-delete-this-directory.txt

# Unit test / coverage reports
htmlcov/
.tox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
.cache
nosetests.xml
coverage.xml
*,cover
.hypothesis/

# Translations
*.mo
*.pot

# Django stuff:
*.log
local_settings.py

# Flask stuff:
instance/
.webassets-cache

# Scrapy stuff:
.scrapy

# Sphinx documentation
docs/_build/

# PyBuilder
/target/

# IPython Notebook
.ipynb_checkpoints

# pyenv
.python-version

# celery beat schedule file
celerybeat-schedule

# dotenv
.env

# virtualenv
venv*/
ENV/

# Spyder project settings
.spyderproject

# Rope project settings
.ropeproject

# Data
*.csv
*.parquet
*.json
*.model
*.png

.idea
example_model.xgb

.DS_Store

.venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary artifact EXTENSIONS -- the belt to the directory rules' braces
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The directory rules at the top are the primary guarantee. These exist for the
# file that lands OUTSIDE data/ results/ models/ logs/ -- a scratch pickle at
# the repo root, a checkpoint saved next to the script that wrote it. That is
# the failure this repository's own history already contains: cached-pickles/
# *.pkl, 26.6 MB plus ~11 copies at 13.2-13.4 MB, inherited from the upstream
# numerai/example-scripts fork. Gone from every branch tip, still in the pack.
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.npy
*.npz
*.joblib
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.onnx
*.safetensors
*.pdf
*.ipynb
cached-pickles/
.pytest_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Negations: the inputs that are NOT regenerable
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FRED-MD is VENDORED, not downloaded: the canonical host
# (files.stlouisfed.org) returns S3 403 from this box, so this copy came from a
# mirror. 595 KB, the positive control for the FARM estimators, and it cannot
# be re-fetched. The README beside it carries the mirror URL and the SHA256 --
# which EXPERIMENTS.md already promises is tracked. Git will not descend into
# an excluded directory, so the directory negation must come first.
!/data/fredmd/
!/data/fredmd/fred-md.csv
!/data/fredmd/README.md

# Cited BY PATH from the e17_ and e48_ runner headers as their method source,
# so it is a dependency rather than an attachment. The other PDF in papers/ is
# cited by author-year only and stays ignored.
!papers/Hyped_ML_paper-21.pdf
